[td][b]"Demon"[/b][/td]
[/tr]
[/table]
[line]
[size=4]What is NOT changed[/size]
[list]
[*][b]No spell balance changes.[/b] Damage, magicka cost, duration and cooldowns are all Enai's, untouched. Enderal keeps all five of Skyrim's magic skills and only renames them, so Triumvirate's spells scale off your Elementalism, Entropy, Light Magic, Mentalism and Psionics with no conversion at all.[/*]
[*][b]No new spells and no removed spells.[/b] All 75 are here. Unlike the Apocalypse conversion, nothing had to be cut for lore: Triumvirate's summons are spirits, ancestors, beasts and Enai's own invented demons, and Enderal's Entropy discipline already raises the dead and binds spirits. There were no Daedra to remove.[/*]
[*][b]No Enderal records rewritten.[/b] See compatibility, below — this is the part I am most pleased with.[/*]
[/list]

For reference, in case you have wondered which Enderal skill governs a Triumvirate spell:

[code]
  Skyrim school     Enderal discipline    Higher school
  Destruction       Elementalism          (its own art)
  Conjuration       Entropy               Sinistra
  Restoration       Light Magic           Thaumaturgy
  Alteration        Mentalism             Thaumaturgy
  Illusion          Psionics              Sinistra[/code]

Note the last two — Alteration is [i]Mentalism[/i] and Illusion is [i]Psionics[/i], not the pairing you would guess.

[code]
  Archetype     Disciplines                              Spells  Staves
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  Druid         Mentalism, Entropy, Light Magic            15       4
  Shadow Mage   Mentalism, Elementalism, Psionics          15       4
  Warlock       Entropy, Elementalism, Psionics            15       8
  Cleric        Elementalism, Psionics, Light Magic        15       4
  Shaman        Mentalism, Entropy, Light Magic            15       6
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
                                                           75      26[/code]
[line]
[size=4]Compatibility and load order[/size]

This [b]is[/b] [font=Courier New]Triumvirate - Mage Archetypes.esp[/font] — it takes the original's place in your load order, exactly where that plugin already sat. It is a full ESP, not ESL-flagged, because it carries all of Triumvirate's own records.

[b]It overrides no container, no NPC, no cell and no faction belonging to Enderal.[/b] Beyond Triumvirate's own records it touches [b]ten records, and all ten are leveled lists that were empty[/b].

That is worth explaining, because it is the reason this mod is unusually safe to install. Enderal ships [b]67 leveled lists named [font=Courier New]<Merchant>_CustomMerchandise[/font][/b] — one per merchant, each already sitting inside that merchant's chest — and [b]every single one of them is empty[/b]. They are an extension point SureAI built and never filled. Putting stock there instead of editing the merchant's chest means:

[list]
[*][b]No conflict with Enderal Gameplay Overhaul.[/b] EGO overrides 319 container records — including three of the ten merchants this mod stocks — but [b]none[/b] of the 67 hooks.[/*]
[*][b]No conflict with my Apocalypse conversion[/b], which stocks six Enderal merchant chests directly.[/*]
[*][b]No conflict with KataPUMB Spell Package[/b], which adds staves to three of them.[/*]
[*][b]No conflict with any other mod using the same hooks[/b], unless it happens to claim the same ten — in which case order them and only the additions are at stake, never a merchant's whole inventory.[/*]
[/list]

If you have used a mod that edits merchant chests and lost half a shop's stock to load order, this is the shape of the fix.

[b]Pinned to Triumvirate 1.8.0.[/b] This ships a rebuilt copy of that exact version's plugin. A newer Triumvirate must not be used with it — install 1.8.0, or wait for this to be refreshed.
[line]
[size=4]Known limitations[/size]

Four of Triumvirate's mechanics lean on vanilla Skyrim perks that Enderal does not have. In every case I chose the behaviour that degrades cleanly over inventing an Enderal perk to stand in, and wrote it down rather than hoping you would not notice:

[list]
[*][b]The Druid's doubled summons never fire.[/b] Twin Souls gates the two-at-once variants of the summon spells. With the perk absent the check is false forever, so the single-summon versions always fire instead. Enderal has no two-summons perk to repoint at.[/*]
[*][b]The Warlock's summons are always base strength.[/b] Same shape: Elemental Potency gates the [i]Potent[/i] variants of all ten conjurations. The base variants carry "does not have the perk", which is now true forever, so they always win. Enderal's Sinistrope line was checked for a substitute — Mystical Binding is summoned [i]weapons[/i], not summoned creatures.[/*]
[*][b]The Shadow Mage's possession never affects Dwarven constructs.[/b] Its condition is "not an automaton OR the target has Master of the Mind". With the perk dead the OR collapses to "not an automaton" — which is exactly vanilla's behaviour for a player who has not taken it.[/*]
[*][b]Three Spirit Guardian variants are unreachable.[/b] Triumvirate ships a guardian per race including Argonian, Khajiit and Orc. Those races exist in Enderal only as unused shells, so no player can be one. The script falls back to the first entry, so [b]every Enderal race gets a guardian[/b] — the three extra actors are simply never selected. Left in place rather than deleted; they are harmless.[/*]
[*][b]Wildshape is untested against Enderal's engine flags.[/b] It calls [font=Courier New]Game.SetBeastForm[/font], an engine-level werewolf flag that cannot be judged by reading records. It is on the test list. If it misbehaves in Enderal, say so and I will look.[/*]
[*][b]Spell tiering follows Enai's ranks, not playtesting against Enderal's curve.[/b] Which merchant sells a spell follows its Triumvirate rank, not a measurement against Enderal's difficulty. Feedback welcome.[/*]
[*][b]Tome names carry no "(Rank N)" suffix[/b], unlike most of Enderal's. That is intentional: in Enderal that suffix means the same spell exists at another strength gated on player level, and Triumvirate spells have exactly one version each. Enderal leaves 13 of its own single-strength tomes unsuffixed for the same reason.[/*]
[*][b]Requires Enderal SE[/b], which is pinned to Skyrim SE [b]1.5.97[/b]. This is a plugin and three loose scripts, so no SKSE version concerns apply to it.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=4]Credits[/size]

[b]Enai Siaion[/b] (with [b]Mihail[/b] for creature assets) — Triumvirate: all 75 spells, the five archetypes, every design decision and every asset. [b]This release is his plugin, modified.[/b] It contains no assets, no spells and no ideas of its own; it exists so his work reaches you in a different game. Redistributed under the mod's stated permissions, which allow modification and re-upload with credit. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/39170]Go and endorse the original[/url] — you need it installed anyway.
[b]SureAI[/b] — Enderal: Forgotten Stories, the two brawl stubs shipped here verbatim, the 67 unused merchant hooks that made the distribution conflict-free, and the written lore every replacement name was taken from.
